\viewkind4\uc1\pard\li288\sl188\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. \tab Where may one find rest and a home for the soul?\cf0 
\par \pard\li720\sl188\slmult0\qj The wings of protection, the peace to console?
\par The world cannot grant me a place where I'm free,
\par \pard\li720\sl188\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par \pard\li720\sl188\slmult0\qj Where sin cannot tempt me dark powers must flee!
\par No, no, no, no, home is not here!
\par The home of the soul is a heavenly sphere!
\par 
\par \pard\li288\sl188\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par     2. \tab Depart from the earth that new home stead to see
\par \pard\li720\sl188\slmult0 A home for the soul bathed in glory and free
\par \pard\li720\sl188\slmult0\qj On high is Jerusalem built of pure gold,
\par \pard\li720\sl188\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par \pard\li720\sl188\slmult0\qj Is this the soul's home that the bride shall be hold?
\par Yes, yes, yes, yes, this is alone,
\par A rest for the soul and a home for God's own!
\par 
\par \pard\li288\sl188\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par     3. \tab How blessed is peace, come from Jesus the light!
\par \pard\li720\sl188\slmult0\qj Death, sin, pain and sorrow must yield to His might
\par The harps shall sound sweetly, in beauty they'll ring,
\par \pard\li720\sl188\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par \pard\li720\sl188\slmult0\qj To souls a glad welcome, a great chorus bring!
\par Rest, rest, rest! rest, heavenly rest!
\par \pard            Make haste to find refuge on our Saviour's breast!\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

